# Testing Rules

Scope: tests for this repository. See [AGENT.md](AGENT.md) for commands and
[docs/features/api-endpoints.md](docs/features/api-endpoints.md) for the
endpoint contracts under test.

## Coverage

- Every endpoint in `app/main.py` must have at least one test in `tests/`.
- Adding or changing an endpoint requires adding or updating its test in the
  same change, including the response fields callers depend on.

## Style

- Tests are async: use `httpx.AsyncClient` with `@pytest.mark.asyncio`, matching
  `tests/test_main.py`:

  ```python
  @pytest.mark.asyncio
  async def test_health_check():
      async with AsyncClient(app=app, base_url="http://test") as client:
          response = await client.get("/health")
          assert response.status_code == 200
  ```

- Assert on status code and on the specific response keys/values.
- Never assert on real secret values — assert on presence and shape only.

## Running tests

Run before every commit:

```bash
pytest
pytest --cov=app
```

## Configuration

Match the pytest config in `pyproject.toml` — do not duplicate or override it
ad hoc:

- `testpaths = ["tests"]`
- `python_files = ["test_*.py"]`, `python_classes = ["Test*"]`,
  `python_functions = ["test_*"]`
- `asyncio_mode = "auto"`
